A minimal agentic-coding harness that runs Claude on a planted-bug repo until
all tests pass OR a turn budget is exhausted. Three required tools:
  - read_file(path) -> str
  - edit_file(path, search, replace) -> {matches: int}
  - run_pytest(args="-q") -> {stdout: str, stderr: str, rc: int}

Loop must:
  1. Call Claude with system prompt + user prompt (failing test) + tool defs.
  2. Dispatch any tool_calls; feed results back as tool_result blocks.
